.TH PLATMON 1 "October 2026" "platmon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
platmon \- view metrics from a platmon service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B platmon
.RI [ host[:port] ]
.RI [ interval ]
.RB [ --once ]
.RB [ --view " view" ]
.br
.B platmon
.RB [ --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
platmon displays platform metrics collected by a running platmon service.
The default host is localhost, the default port is 9797, and the default
update interval is one second. The interval must be a finite positive number.
On an interactive terminal, the client displays a live screen.
Redirected output uses plain text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --once
Print one snapshot and exit without clearing the screen.
.TP
.BI --view " view"
Select the initial interactive view: overview, resources, network, storage,
thermal, power, or system. This option cannot be combined with --once.
.TP
.B --help
Display command usage and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display the client version and exit.
.SH KEYS
In the live screen, keys 1 through 7 select views.
Tab and the arrow keys switch views; q quits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to a nonempty value to disable colors.
.TP
.B PLATMON_ASCII
Set to 1 to draw using ASCII characters.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/platmon/platmon.ini
Service configuration, including the listening address and port.
The client takes its target address from the command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B platmon --once
.br
.B platmon 192.168.1.10:9797 2
.br
.B platmon --view power
.SH NOTES
The Debian package provides platmon.service.
After changing service configuration, restart it with
.BR "sudo systemctl restart platmon" .
The HTTP API is unauthenticated; use it on a trusted network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
